  "title": "Consonants review: look-alikes",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "You can now recognize every consonant in the chart: **ক খ গ ঘ ঙ · চ ছ জ ঝ ঞ · ট ঠ ড ঢ ণ · ত থ দ ধ ন · প ফ ব ভ ম · য র ল · শ ষ স হ · ড় ঢ় য় ৎ ং ঃ ঁ**.\n\n**Shape look-alikes**: ব (triangle) vs র (triangle + dot); ধ (open top-left) vs থ (bottom loop) vs য; উ (vowel) vs ড (notch in the top line); ড vs ড় and য vs য় (the dot!).\n\n**Sound-alikes**: জ/য, ন/ণ, শ/ষ/স and ঙ/ং sound the same. You can't hear the difference, so learn each word's spelling.\n\n**Puff pairs**: ক/খ, চ/ছ, ট/ঠ, ত/থ, প/ফ. Listen for the breath. Next up: vowel signs, which let you read whole words like মামা and খালা.",
